- In every search-phase state (s = 11 with the search task, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8) your action sets the altitude alt for the next step: keep (stay at the current altitude), low, med or high. In all other states (4, 5, 9, 10, 12, and 11 when following), the action has no effect.
- The water visibility limits the altitude: poor visibility (water_visib 1..2) allows low; average visibility (water_visib 3..5) allows low or med; good visibility (water_visib 6..10) allows low or med or high. Requesting a higher altitude than allowed gives the highest allowed one, so falling visibility forces the AUV down.
